 and unlabeled data using graph mincuts</article-title><conf-name>In Proceedings of the 18th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML '01)</conf-name><conf-date>June-July 2001</conf-date><conf-loc>Williamstown, Mass, USA</conf-loc><publisher-name>Morgan Kaufmann</publisher-name><fpage>19</fpage><lpage>26</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Joachims</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transductive learning via spectral graph partitioning</article-title><year>2003</year><month>8</month><conf-name>In Proceedings of the 20th International Conference on Machine Learning (ICML '03), vol.1</conf-name><conf-loc>Washington, DC, USA</conf-loc><fpage>290</fpage><lpage>297</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bennett</surname><given-names>KP</given-names></name><name><surname>Demiriz</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Semi-supervised support vector machines</article-title><source><italic>Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 11</italic></source><year>1998</year><volume>2</volume><publisher-name>The MIT Press</publisher-name><fpage>368</fpage><lpage>374</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blanchard</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Blankertz</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>BCI competition 2003-data set IIa: spatial patterns of self-controlled brain rhythm modulations</article-title><source><italic>IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering</italic></source><year>2004</year><volume>51</volume><issue>6</issue><fpage>1062</fpage><lpage>1066</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15188879</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ramoser</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000fc;ller-Gerking</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pfurtscheller</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Optimal spatial filtering of single trial EEG during imagined hand movement</article-title><source><italic>IEEE Transactions on Rehabilitation Engineering</italic></source><year>2000</year><volume>8</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>441</fpage><lpage>446</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11204034</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="confproc"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Guan</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Qin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Enhancing feature extraction with sparse component analysis for brain-computer interface</article-title><conf-name>In Proceedings of the 27th IEEE Annual International Conference of Engineering in Medicine and Biology (EMBS '05), vol.7</conf-name><conf-date>September 2005</conf-date><conf-loc>Shanghai, China</conf-loc><fpage>5335</fpage><lpage>5338</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Wolpaw</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>McFarland</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Neat</surname><given-names>GW</given-names></name><name><surname>Forneris</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An EEG-based brain-computer interface for cursor control</article-title><source><italic>Electroencephalography and Clinical Neurophysiology</italic></source><year>1991</year><volume>78</volume><issue>3</issue